126: Widget build(BuildContext context) {
127:   final l10n = context.l10n;
128:   return Text(l10n.helloWorld);
129: }
130: ```
131: 
132: ### Adding Supported Locales
133: 
134: Update the `CFBundleLocalizations` array in the `Info.plist` at `ios/Runner/Info.plist` to include the new locale.
135: 
136: ```xml
137:     ...
138: 
139:     <key>CFBundleLocalizations</key>
140: 	<array>
141: 		<string>en</string>
142: 		<string>es</string>
143: 	</array>
144: 
145:     ...
146: ```
147: 
148: ### Adding Translations
149: 
150: 1. For each supported locale, add a new ARB file in `lib/l10n/arb`.
151: 
152: ```
153: ├── l10n
154: │   ├── arb
155: │   │   ├── app_en.arb
156: │   │   └── app_es.arb
157: ```
158: 
159: 2. Add the translated strings to each `.arb` file:
160: 
161: `app_en.arb`
162: 
163: ```arb
164: {
165:     "@@locale": "en",
166:     "counterAppBarTitle": "Counter",
167:     "@counterAppBarTitle": {
168:         "description": "Text shown in the AppBar of the Counter Page"
169:     }
170: }
171: ```
172: 
173: `app_es.arb`
174: 
175: ```arb
176: {
177:     "@@locale": "es",
178:     "counterAppBarTitle": "Contador",
179:     "@counterAppBarTitle": {
180:         "description": "Texto mostrado en la AppBar de la página del contador"
181:     }
182: }
183: ```
184: 
185: ### Generating Translations
186: 
187: To use the latest translations changes, you will need to generate them:
188: 
189: 1. Generate localizations for the current project:
190: 
191: ```sh
192: flutter gen-l10n --arb-dir="lib/l10n/arb"
193: ```
194: 
195: Alternatively, run `flutter run` and code generation will take place automatically.
